{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/916605-how-do-services-work","id":916605,"title":"How Do Services Work?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-17T20:40:04-07:00","id":916605,"title":"How Do Services Work?","content":"What does the Die bonus for services mean? You add that bonus to your own roll? What about situations where the contractor is performing the task instead of you? Do they have a dice pool equal to yours +x?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T16:37:41-07:00","id":917033,"title":"","content":"I would assume it would apply to whichever die roll you procured it for, whether it's yourself or another's. If you are attempting the action it modifies, you get the bonus. If another player is attempting the roll (but you're paying for the service), they get the bonus. If an NPC is performing an action on your behalf that requires a roll, and you supplement their attempt with the service, the bonus gets added to their roll. If the roll ends up being a more abstract action, or some sort of Down &amp; Dirty amalgam, the bonus should apply to that roll. The intent is that it's a one-time circumstantial bonus gained from using another person's expertise to modify your own action, and in most cases it's probably transferable to a willing proxy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T19:44:43-07:00","id":917109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/916605-how-do-services-work?p=917033#post917033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If an NPC is performing an action on your behalf that requires a roll, and you supplement their attempt with the service, the bonus gets added to their roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>This doesn't make sense. If I hire a chauffer, we're not going to both be driving the car at the same time. If I or my ally are driving the car, he's not going to be sitting in the back seat barking orders to me. So then what is the +2 bonus in the book supposed to apply to? The chauffer should have his own dice pool, but the book says nothing about this.<br /> <br /> Same goes for stuff like Rush Plastic Surgery. I'm not going to perform plastic surgery on myself. The doctor I hired is. If I hire someone to steal a protected relic, they're going to be doing the job, not me. So where does this +3 bonus apply?<br /> <br /> For half of these &quot;Services&quot;, the contractor is performing the job entirely by themselves. They're not training you or just assisting you. In these cases, I'd expect the book to give some way of calculating the NPC's dice pool, but that's completely absent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T21:25:58-07:00","id":917158,"title":"","content":"No, this would be referring to separate NPCs: the primary actor, and the supplementing actor providing the service. If the primary actor is a PC, that actor gets the roll, modified by the service provided. We're not talking about combat-scale instant actions, but extended actions that take time and are rolled for at the culmination of the effort, in most cases. Keep in mind too that it's often not a singular character providing a service, but could be anything from an office to a corporation.<br /> <br /> If a service is contracted, and that contractor is present in the scene, that character should be statted out as is appropriate, if their skills matter that much. A chauffeur who is just driving the character around town doesn't really need a dice pool to be figured out, but instead offers the +2 bonus to Social rolls because he gets the character to appointments on time, reduces stress, and impresses onlookers. If things go sour, the chauffeur might need a dice pool figured out for Drive or whatever. <br /> <br /> And you do have a starting base for what that dice pool looks like. 2 dice is considered the human statistical average, and each service has an associated Skill. If you need to decide what that pool looks like, the chauffeur likely has 4 dice. The rush plastic surgeon probably has the same, though the ST could and should alter these pools as the character requires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T21:44:27-07:00","id":917172,"title":"","content":"Think of services as equipment with a transitory bonus. You are having trouble translating the ancient Egyptian hyroglyphs so you call up your historical linguist buddy at the university and his advice is good for a +2 on your roll to translate them. You want that fuckhead Steve to get out of town, so you hire a PI to dig up some dirt on him and the information he finds counts as +2 Hard Leverage on your roll to blackmail him. You're performing a ritual to banish an unwelcome ghost so you call in an exorcist and his help is worth +2 on the roll. Etc. generally you'll have a specific task in mind that you're hiring a service to assist you in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T22:03:44-07:00","id":917178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/916605-how-do-services-work?p=917172#post917172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think of services as equipment with a transitory bonus. You are having trouble translating the ancient Egyptian hyroglyphs so you call up your historical linguist buddy at the university and his advice is good for a +2 on your roll to translate them. You want that fuckhead Steve to get out of town, so you hire a PI to dig up some dirt on him and the information he finds counts as +2 Hard Leverage on your roll to blackmail him. You're performing a ritual to banish an unwelcome ghost so you call in an exorcist and his help is worth +2 on the roll. Etc. generally you'll have a specific task in mind that you're hiring a service to assist you in.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense for some of the services, but there's plenty of example services that don't fit that mold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T22:13:56-07:00","id":917186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/916605-how-do-services-work?p=917178#post917178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That makes sense for some of the services, but there's plenty of example services that don't fit that mold.</div> </div> </div> </div>Give me one, I'll see if I can think of a way to use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T01:59:47-07:00","id":917243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/916605-how-do-services-work?p=917186#post917186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Give me one, I'll see if I can think of a way to use it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I mentioned chauffer, which gives a +2 to Drive. Or Rush Plastic Surgery which gives a +3 to Medicine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T02:17:25-07:00","id":917253,"title":"","content":"The bonus dice aren't inherently limited to the Skill in question. Like any equipment it can apply to any action that makes sense. <br /> <br /> The chauffer could easily be a bonus to carousing; as an example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T11:51:26-07:00","id":917476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/916605-how-do-services-work?p=917243#post917243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I mentioned chauffer, which gives a +2 to Drive. Or Rush Plastic Surgery which gives a +3 to Medicine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Verge already gave some great suggestions of what types of rolls the bonus from a chauffeur might apply to. For a specific example, let's say you want to try intimidating that fuckhead Steve before you resort to outright blackmailing him. You hire a chauffeur to drive you to his workplace in a limo so you can glare menacingly at him out the back window as the car keeps pace with him, &quot;offer&quot; to give him a ride home and &quot;recommend&quot; that he take a long vacation &quot;for his health.&quot; The +2 bonus could apply to the roll to increase the impression from Good to Excellent. If that succeeds, all you need is to offer to pay for a one-way plane ticket and you've got a Perfect impression, no need to use that Hard Leverage the PI dug up for you. But it's in your back pocket just in case you really need it.<br /> <br /> Rush Plastic Surgery is an easy one. You're wanted for some crime and you want to disappear, so you pay a shady surgeon to fuck up your face enough to give you a +3 bonus on rolls to avoid being recognized by the police.<br /> <br /> As Heavy Arms said, the example Services are sorted by Skill to make it easier to find something appropriate, just like any other equipment, the bonus can apply to any appropriate roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T12:37:19-07:00","id":917499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/916605-how-do-services-work?p=917243#post917243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rush Plastic Surgery, which gives a +2 to Medicine.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you have Medicine (Plastic Surgery) yourself, the bonus can reflect access to a surgical suite tailored to that purpose (that's assuming you're renting on short notice, of course, and not just buying it outright as Equipment). It could also reflect another surgeon working with you, combining expertise, another pair of hands so they can nip while you tuck.<br /> <br /> If you're getting an emergency face-ectomy before the mob catches up to you, apply the bonus to whatever disguise you're using for your new identity.<br /> <br /> Or just use it as a penalty for attempts to place your age for a few years.<br /> <br /> Edit: Ninja'd<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1289,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","user":"Hastur00","date":". 06-19-2016, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T15:58:43-07:00","id":917592,"title":"","content":"The Services is a means to price a service, rate its benefits in game terms, and allow the transaction to be played out offscreen without worrying about details. Being listed as &quot;equipment&quot; is meant to drive this home: services are tools. Yeah, there are people involved, but they are parceled with the service, not the other way around. If you wanted a chauffeur with a Drive Skill whose personal characteristics <i>matter</i>, that falls under Retainer (which also provides a handy resolution to the dice pool question), where Allies might cover the surgeon. Services are one-offs, though, and they overlap with the Merit Buddies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}